101
00:09:46.040 --> 00:09:56.280
[George] When Governor Altgeld protested that federal intervention was unconstitutional and an invasion of states' rights, Cleveland delivered his immortal executive decree.

102
00:09:56.280 --> 00:10:02.360
[George] If it takes the entire Army and Navy of the United States to deliver a postal card in Chicago.

103
00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:14.040
[George] On July 3, 1894, President Cleveland ordered 12,000 regular United States Army soldiers, commanded by Major General Nelson A.

104
00:10:14.040 --> 00:10:20.120
[George] Miles, to march into Chicago with fixed bayonets, cavalry sabers, and gatling guns.

105
00:10:20.120 --> 00:10:26.920
[George] Bloody riots erupted between soldiers and strikers, leaving 30 civilians dead and dozens wounded.

106
00:10:26.920 --> 00:10:29.080
[George] But the military broke the strike.

107
00:10:29.080 --> 00:10:29.960
[George] Eugene V.

108
