121
00:11:54.480 --> 00:12:02.320
[George] Surrounded by his beloved wife Frances and his children, Cleveland whispered his final words to the physician who leaned over his bed.

122
00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.800
[George] I have tried so hard to do right.

123
00:12:04.800 --> 00:12:10.000
[George] It was the simple, unvarnished epitaph of an immovable American president.

124
00:12:10.000 --> 00:12:22.480
[George] Backslash and backslash and Cleveland's final years in Princeton were marked by quiet intellectual reflection, as former adversaries gradually recognized his incorruptible integrity and moral fortitude.

125
00:12:22.480 --> 00:12:31.800
[George] He served as a trustee of Princeton University, maintaining his belief that honest public service required immovable adherence to principle.

126
00:12:29.920 --> 00:12:36.600
[George] Grover Cleveland's second term remains a masterclass in executive resolve.

127
00:12:36.760 --> 00:12:44.360
[Rebecca] By bearing personal agony in silence and standing firm against civil unrest, he preserved the stability of the American Republic.

